  "failed_symbols lists every unit whose verificationOutcome was not SATISFIED (1 UNSATISFIED + 2 PENDING/CONTESTED); unsatisfied_count counts only UNSATISFIED rows. CONTESTED means canonical OGR REQUIRED but runtime reported no obligation (src/verification/accounting/run_accounting.nim:725-729).",
  "An AXIOM_STATE_DIR that contains nothing but directories fails closed: `bin/ax prove` exits 2 with `loadKernelScope fail-closed: lock file missing at '/tmp/stage2-state-full/data/verification_scope.lock'` (preserved as full_fresh_empty_state_attempt.log, sha256 5ce05704e2ef3c3838421d2db25d542ed4de4f7cffac7389748d46c94e1e9c4c). Both fresh state dirs were therefore seeded with only the immutable contract inputs data/verification_scope.lock and data/baseline.json, copied byte-identically from commit 983e836, exactly as .github/workflows/byo-agent.yml:217-226 does; these two seeded inputs appear in state_files.",
  "The CLI printed no JSON verdict/state on stdout for these in-repo runs; evidence was read from $AXIOM_STATE_DIR/logs/ax_proof_state.json (outputJson is populated only in external-subject mode, src/cli/axiom_engine.nim:6086-6088).",
  "Warm CI-scope did NOT reuse certificates: runAccounting.satisfiedByReused=0, reuseEligibleRowCount=0, summary.solverInvocationCount=1, and the cert was rewritten (identical bytes, sha256 bae2e26c5a740dab7e31076a3048f4825d37f56b87608d00d8fdfb608a384a41). The read vault is repo-relative data/trusted/certificates while writes go to $AXIOM_STATE_DIR/build/certificates (src/verification/cert_vault_role.nim:21-29, axiom_engine.nim:5366). Warm speedup (70s -> 28s) came from topology/graph caches: topology log line 5 changed from '2562 changed' to '570 changed'.",
  "Full-scope (no --target) is not 'all 40 kernel symbols': the eligibility gate admitted 5 proof candidates out of 16163 topology candidates / |Kernel|=40, excluding 12 non-proof-candidate symbols (full_fresh.log:19); firstIntCore was excluded with semantics.unresolved-fact (full_fresh.log:15).",
  "The full-scope log's IR pipeline 'Proof Summary: Total 4 / Pass 2 / Fail 2' (full_fresh.log:40-43) counts IR-extracted entries, not the 5 canonical run-accounting units.",
